WEBVTT

00:02.690 --> 00:04.980
We'll work things out here.

00:04.980 --> 00:06.640
The rest of you, go on ahead!

00:09.610 --> 00:11.070
Shannon, gun it!

00:16.820 --> 00:17.910
Sorry to disappoint.

00:17.910 --> 00:19.370
But just ahead...

00:21.500 --> 00:22.960
is a pitfall.

00:25.340 --> 00:27.210
If we fall from here—

00:30.380 --> 00:32.430
<b><i>HE'S DEAD</i></b>

00:42.190 --> 00:43.080
<b>THE</b>

00:43.080 --> 00:43.620
<b>LEGEN</b>

00:43.620 --> 00:44.120
<b>DARY</b>

00:44.120 --> 00:44.580
<b>HERO</b>

00:44.580 --> 00:45.080
<b>IS</b>

00:45.040 --> 00:45.540
<b>DEAD</b>

01:59.010 --> 02:02.510
<b>Episode 8</b>

01:59.010 --> 02:02.510
<b>The Legendary Hero Is a Student!</b>

02:00.050 --> 02:02.510
The shortest route to Elvania...

02:02.510 --> 02:05.860
I knew that if I set a trap here, 
you'd fall right into it.

02:05.860 --> 02:08.980
Of course, I'm sure this won't be the end of them.

02:09.360 --> 02:12.310
It'd take more than a pit trap 
to kill the legendary hero.

02:15.140 --> 02:17.010
Hey, you okay?!

02:17.010 --> 02:19.090
Honestly, a pitfall?

02:19.090 --> 02:21.470
This is quite unfunny for a prank, you know.

02:21.470 --> 02:22.950
I didn't dig this one, damn it!

02:23.950 --> 02:24.790
What is this?

02:24.790 --> 02:28.250
I adjusted the Sacred Sword's 
rigidity to use it as a cushion.

02:28.570 --> 02:29.750
Hey, hang on!

02:29.750 --> 02:32.030
Since when could you use 
the Sacred Sword, Sis?!

02:32.030 --> 02:32.590
Erk!

02:32.590 --> 02:35.050
I-It's part of Sion's power!

02:35.050 --> 02:37.760
He can let anyone use the Sacred Sword!

02:37.760 --> 02:40.720
I've never heard of a power 
like that before...

02:40.720 --> 02:43.050
Hey, you think we should get out of here?

02:43.050 --> 02:45.780
Whoever set the trap is
probably on their way.

02:45.780 --> 02:49.390
But with the enchanted
carriage in this state...

02:49.390 --> 02:51.570
There appears to be a city nearby.

02:51.570 --> 02:53.110
Shall we head in that direction?

02:53.110 --> 02:54.290
Might as well.

02:54.290 --> 02:58.820
We could find a new ride there
or someone to fix this one.

03:01.320 --> 03:02.780
The fog is so thick...

03:03.170 --> 03:05.280
Which way should we go?

03:05.280 --> 03:08.450
My Sacred Sword can blow 
this fog away, no problem!

03:11.410 --> 03:13.290
Okay, let's get going!

03:13.290 --> 03:14.490
H-Hang on!

03:14.490 --> 03:16.880
There might be more traps around!

03:16.880 --> 03:19.120
Aw, what a worrywart!

03:19.120 --> 03:21.260
The chance of there 
being more traps here is...

03:22.220 --> 03:23.550
high!

03:23.550 --> 03:25.800
Do you have something against Dame Milly?!

03:25.800 --> 03:27.150
I'm tellin' you it ain't me!

03:27.150 --> 03:28.980
Milly! Get back here already!

03:28.980 --> 03:30.490
Yeah, roger that!

03:30.490 --> 03:33.260
Woman. Looks tasty. Meat.

03:33.600 --> 03:35.210
Oh, not again!

03:35.210 --> 03:37.150
Milly! You okay?

03:37.150 --> 03:40.640
Big Sis, there's devils in the fog!

03:40.640 --> 03:41.670
You're okay—

03:41.670 --> 03:43.200
Or not!

03:43.650 --> 03:45.670
The most terrible devils!

03:45.670 --> 03:47.630
They did this and that and 
the other thing to me...

03:47.630 --> 03:49.160
You sure it wasn't some perv?

03:49.160 --> 03:50.570
Okay, next we'll send out Margueri—

03:50.570 --> 03:51.620
I am not going!

03:52.500 --> 03:55.770
This place is even more 
dangerous than I thought.

03:55.770 --> 03:58.880
I'll bet you this fog's an enemy spell, too.

03:58.880 --> 04:01.400
<i>And there are traps all around.</i>

04:01.400 --> 04:03.930
<i>This ain't how devils fights.</i>

04:04.350 --> 04:09.140
<i>Though it's hard to believe that necromancer
guy would play like this either...</i>

04:10.040 --> 04:12.350
This devil's mist spell

04:12.350 --> 04:16.600
allows only an authorized few 
to see through the fog.

04:16.940 --> 04:20.920
I can spy on everything you're doing.

04:21.390 --> 04:23.360
Now, what's your next move?

04:23.670 --> 04:25.120
You sure about this?

04:25.120 --> 04:28.650
Surely even Sion the hero 
isn't impervious to traps...

04:28.650 --> 04:29.950
Don't you worry.

04:29.950 --> 04:32.580
It'll take more than a trap 
to take out this legendary hero.

04:32.980 --> 04:34.610
I see.

04:34.610 --> 04:37.840
So the rumor that the legendary 
hero is dead is true.

04:38.180 --> 04:41.070
A corpse could indeed survive 
any trap I throw at it.

04:41.070 --> 04:43.800
And that cautious cross-shaped formation...

04:44.450 --> 04:46.880
I can tell they're reasonably intelligent.

04:47.370 --> 04:48.260
But...

04:48.900 --> 04:50.110
that won't be enough.

04:50.780 --> 04:52.560
This fog is magical.

04:53.000 --> 04:55.020
It can even cloak someone's presence.

05:00.150 --> 05:01.300
Marguerite!

05:01.300 --> 05:02.280
Your Highness!

05:02.890 --> 05:04.400
That's one down.

05:04.400 --> 05:05.720
Move out of the way.

05:05.720 --> 05:06.810
I can—

05:08.410 --> 05:10.240
Hey, what happened?!

05:10.240 --> 05:12.010
You guys are still alive out there, right?

05:12.010 --> 05:13.800
Talk to me!

05:16.550 --> 05:18.490
No way...

05:18.490 --> 05:21.430
They can't all just be dead...

05:25.580 --> 05:28.030
Damn it. This is nuts.

05:28.030 --> 05:31.120
Please, spare me! I surrender!

05:31.120 --> 05:33.180
You can hear me, can't you?!

05:33.180 --> 05:35.610
Whoever's the leader out there!

05:36.940 --> 05:39.060
We took 'em all out.

05:39.060 --> 05:41.190
Yes, I saw everything.

05:41.190 --> 05:44.150
This is the last one.

05:44.150 --> 05:46.790
The moment you see your allies fallen,

05:46.790 --> 05:49.260
you pathetically plead for your life.

05:49.260 --> 05:51.670
A selfish lowlife like you
wielding the Sacred Sword...

05:51.670 --> 05:53.370
What sort of farce is this?

05:53.370 --> 05:55.440
I... I'll give you the Sacred Sword!

05:55.440 --> 05:56.330
Just spare me!

05:56.330 --> 05:58.450
Willing to give up the sword, are you?

05:58.450 --> 06:02.580
Terribly sorry,
but I can't take you at your word.

06:02.580 --> 06:05.130
Prove you're serious and I'll consider it.

06:07.780 --> 06:09.970
Is that enough? Please...

06:09.970 --> 06:15.430
<i>You're that desperate to survive, 
even after seeing all your allies slain?</i>

06:16.020 --> 06:17.400
Very well.

06:17.400 --> 06:20.340
I'll gladly take the Sacred Sword.

06:20.340 --> 06:23.740
But I fear I must also ask you to die.

06:24.230 --> 06:26.620
No way! You promised!

06:26.620 --> 06:28.700
I only said I'd <i>consider</i> it.

06:28.700 --> 06:31.620
Sorry to inform you, 
but I'm a bit of a fiend!

06:32.160 --> 06:35.370
In that case, go ahead and get her, Anri.

06:36.870 --> 06:38.330
It can't be...

06:38.330 --> 06:40.660
They aren't dead?!

06:41.050 --> 06:43.000
Hey, what happened to your backside?

06:43.000 --> 06:44.840
That devil did it!

06:44.840 --> 06:47.510
You made me play dead for so long...

06:47.510 --> 06:49.260
Possession necromancy?!

06:49.720 --> 06:54.680
Anri manipulated that devil and 
pretended to go around killing everyone.

06:54.680 --> 06:57.140
We used art supplies for the blood!

06:57.140 --> 07:00.680
When that devil closed in to try to stab me,

07:00.680 --> 07:02.570
I countered and slew it!

07:02.570 --> 07:04.340
You didn't notice, did you?

07:04.340 --> 07:06.730
It happened someplace
you couldn't see.

07:06.730 --> 07:09.730
<i>Was that the purpose of their formation?</i>

07:09.730 --> 07:12.820
<i>They weren't just wary of the devils?</i>

07:12.820 --> 07:17.900
But the only way you could pull that off 
is if you knew where I was!

07:17.900 --> 07:19.910
That was the easiest part of all.

07:19.910 --> 07:23.630
I had eyes on you and what you
were doing the entire time.

07:23.630 --> 07:27.940
Once we knew your positions, we merely 
had to make myself the clear target.

07:27.940 --> 07:30.640
And since you were watching 
from your lofty perch,

07:30.640 --> 07:32.270
I pegged you for the ringleader.

07:32.270 --> 07:36.520
I know all about the kind of person
who fights with traps.

07:36.520 --> 07:38.510
They're cautious above all.

07:38.510 --> 07:40.980
They don't fight unless it's a sure bet.

07:40.980 --> 07:47.280
So to lure you out, we had to create a setup
where you'd be confident of your victory.

07:47.280 --> 07:50.840
And you walked right into our trap!

07:50.840 --> 07:54.120
I mean, if you wanna try to outtrap me,

07:54.120 --> 07:55.910
you need another century of training!

07:55.910 --> 07:59.130
But the princess and Anri 
did most of the work, right?

08:02.160 --> 08:06.710
<b>X-Ray</b>

08:02.490 --> 08:06.710
Hey, while we're at it, she's got 
a pretty nice set of thighs.

08:06.710 --> 08:07.540
Tou—

08:07.540 --> 08:09.910
Yuna, the fog appears to have lifted,

08:09.910 --> 08:12.580
so you have no further need 
to use the X-Ray spell.

08:12.580 --> 08:15.430
Er, I thought she might be hiding weapons!

08:15.810 --> 08:19.180
Now then, I'm no fan of pointless killing.

08:19.180 --> 08:23.390
Strip down, slip on some stockings, plant your nose
in the dirt, and maybe I'll forgive you!

08:23.390 --> 08:28.250
Big Sis... Has Touka's influence 
corrupted you to that extent?

08:28.250 --> 08:30.610
It's like we're the bad guys 
here or something.

08:30.610 --> 08:33.080
Well, what's it gonna be?

08:33.080 --> 08:34.070
Tell me—

08:34.070 --> 08:36.220
Agh! I'm so sorry!

08:36.220 --> 08:37.060
What?!

08:37.480 --> 08:40.540
Wh-What are you doing here...

08:40.890 --> 08:42.090
Master?

08:43.880 --> 08:46.000
Touka's master?

08:46.000 --> 08:47.930
Ethel Borgnine.

08:46.000 --> 08:52.710
<b>Ethel Borgnine
Thief, Touka's Master</b>

08:47.930 --> 08:52.710
She taught me how to make traps 
and general survival knowledge.

08:52.710 --> 08:54.370
It's been so long, Mast—

08:54.370 --> 08:55.690
Clothes on, please.

08:55.690 --> 08:56.860
"Master"?

08:56.860 --> 09:00.010
I don't ever recall having a student
like you.

09:01.470 --> 09:02.720
<i>Son of a bitch!</i>

09:02.720 --> 09:03.930
I knew it!

09:03.930 --> 09:05.440
So that's what's going on.

09:05.900 --> 09:09.350
I should have caught on the minute you 
said anything about stockings...

09:09.350 --> 09:10.330
Big Sis—

09:10.330 --> 09:13.010
I mean... That's you, isn't it,
Big Brother Touka?

09:13.360 --> 09:14.820
That's Touka?

09:14.820 --> 09:16.940
Anri. The Coffin of the Living.

09:16.940 --> 09:18.070
V-Very well.

09:19.530 --> 09:20.940
Touka?!

09:20.940 --> 09:22.490
It's possession necromancy.

09:22.490 --> 09:24.350
Which means my sister...

09:24.350 --> 09:26.510
Don't worry. She's not dead.

09:26.510 --> 09:27.960
I'll catch you up later.

09:27.960 --> 09:31.880
Did you meet your master during 
that period you mentioned

09:31.880 --> 09:35.090
when Farom and Arat were at war?

09:35.090 --> 09:35.970
Yeah.

09:35.970 --> 09:38.760
Though by that point, 
the Gates of Hell had opened,

09:38.760 --> 09:41.250
and both sides had bigger 
things to worry about.

09:41.250 --> 09:45.310
Ah, so your strategic brilliance 
has a mysterious origin!

09:45.990 --> 09:48.240
I guess it was three and a half years ago...

09:48.240 --> 09:52.270
My parents were dead, 
and I was trying to get back to Elvania

09:52.270 --> 09:54.990
when I fell into one of Master's traps.

09:54.990 --> 09:57.420
Running away was about 
all I was good for back then.

09:57.420 --> 09:59.400
That trap could've killed me, and yet...

09:59.400 --> 10:02.080
I was so impressed by it.

10:02.330 --> 10:04.790
<b>Several Days Later</b>

10:04.790 --> 10:08.720
I didn't set that trap 
to catch children, you know.

10:11.090 --> 10:12.210
A kid like you

10:12.210 --> 10:14.910
going all the way to Elvania alone
in the state the world's in?

10:14.910 --> 10:16.460
That'll never happen.

10:16.820 --> 10:19.520
Then take me there, why don't you?

10:19.520 --> 10:21.010
I can pay you, at least a little...

10:21.790 --> 10:24.300
What do I want with a babysitting job?

10:24.300 --> 10:25.600
Don't be ridiculous.

10:25.600 --> 10:27.730
Then take me as your student!

10:27.730 --> 10:29.520
With skills like yours, even if I'm alone...

10:32.140 --> 10:34.730
I'm a fugitive with a bounty on my head.

10:34.730 --> 10:37.720
If you don't want to die, 
get out of my sight, kid.

10:45.070 --> 10:46.160
Please.

10:46.160 --> 10:48.460
I really need to get back.

10:49.450 --> 10:51.670
But why ask a villain like me?

10:53.010 --> 10:54.210
So be it.

10:55.070 --> 10:58.630
On the way to Elvania, 
I'll teach you everything I know.

10:59.040 --> 11:00.810
But remember, I'm a villain.

11:00.810 --> 11:02.640
Forget that, and I'll kill you.

11:03.110 --> 11:06.720
Master whipped me into shape 
on the way back to Elvania.

11:06.720 --> 11:08.800
We made it there in a few months' time.

11:08.800 --> 11:12.270
Of course! So <i>you're</i> the one 
who killed the legendary hero!

11:12.270 --> 11:14.690
What?! What's the meaning of this, Big Bro?!

11:14.690 --> 11:16.870
I-It's not like that! It was an accident!

11:16.870 --> 11:19.860
He just walked into my trap and died!

11:19.860 --> 11:21.140
The real question here...

11:21.140 --> 11:24.320
is why you're working with the guys
siding with the devils, Master.

11:24.320 --> 11:27.290
They're trying to wipe out humanity.

11:27.290 --> 11:30.750
I was at the Gates of Hell three months ago.

11:31.180 --> 11:33.390
It changed my way of thinking.

11:33.390 --> 11:36.710
I've decided to help out with 
their little revenge plot.

11:36.710 --> 11:38.410
That ain't a real explanation.

11:38.410 --> 11:41.680
What's going on at the Gates of Hell?

11:42.040 --> 11:43.690
Go there, and you'll see.

11:43.690 --> 11:44.720
Huh?

11:44.720 --> 11:46.970
You too, necromancer.

11:46.970 --> 11:49.660
Go there, see it for yourself,

11:49.660 --> 11:50.930
and decide.

11:51.280 --> 11:54.650
What will you choose, 
and what will you cut loose?

11:54.650 --> 11:56.920
Wh-Where are you going, Master?

11:56.920 --> 12:00.670
Since you're really Touka,
I'll let you go. This time.

12:00.670 --> 12:03.240
But I'm still taking the Sacred Sword.

12:03.700 --> 12:07.130
Though if you want a fight to 
the death, I'm ready and willing.

12:07.130 --> 12:09.950
I'm fairly certain I can kill all of you.

12:09.950 --> 12:11.510
Give me a damn break!

12:11.510 --> 12:14.820
You bust up our enchanted carriage,
and now you're walking off with the sword?!

12:14.820 --> 12:16.600
I <i>am</i> a thief.

12:16.600 --> 12:19.420
I won't give up a treasure like this readily.

12:20.470 --> 12:23.120
Fine. You can have the sword.

12:23.120 --> 12:25.900
In exchange, come with us 
to the Gates of Hell.

12:25.900 --> 12:28.310
With you at our side, we'll be unbeatable!

12:28.310 --> 12:30.770
Have you forgotten that we're enemies?

12:30.770 --> 12:33.480
Well, I'm not asking you to do it for free.

12:33.480 --> 12:35.940
It'll be in exchange for your right arm.

12:36.340 --> 12:41.050
I inserted a pin into the hilt
that channels a lightning spell.

12:41.050 --> 12:43.900
Drop it, or you're asking for a direct hit.

12:43.900 --> 12:47.800
I see. You don't miss a beat, do you?

12:47.800 --> 12:50.870
But why tell me before using the spell?

12:51.160 --> 12:53.580
Because I trust you.

12:54.010 --> 12:56.190
I told you we're enemies.

12:56.190 --> 12:57.370
Fine.

12:57.370 --> 12:58.540
I lose.

12:59.260 --> 13:02.040
There's a magical craftsman's 
workshop to the northeast.

13:02.040 --> 13:04.380
You should be able
to fix your carriage there.

13:04.380 --> 13:06.330
Aw, that's my master for ya!

13:06.330 --> 13:07.550
You're so darn nice!

13:07.550 --> 13:09.600
I just knew you'd cooperate!

13:09.600 --> 13:10.760
Although...

13:10.760 --> 13:12.430
There's more to it, y'know?

13:13.450 --> 13:15.810
You accepted defeat.

13:15.810 --> 13:21.380
That means you gotta offer up your life
or accept some other condition, right?

13:21.900 --> 13:23.790
Of course, we're all friends here, Master.

13:23.790 --> 13:25.800
I won't force you into anything.

13:25.800 --> 13:31.370
But I'd be <i>real</i> disappointed to find out 
my dear master isn't a woman of her word!

13:32.370 --> 13:35.130
You piece-of-shit student!

13:35.130 --> 13:39.170
The minute you're back 
in your own body, you'll pay!

13:39.170 --> 13:41.860
You may wish to watch your back as well.

13:46.800 --> 13:49.490
I can't believe they won her over.

13:49.490 --> 13:51.640
The power of lushighs is impressive indeed!

13:52.010 --> 13:53.600
Why didn't you tell me?

13:54.600 --> 13:59.590
I thought ignorance would make 
the reunion all the more touching.

13:59.590 --> 14:02.570
Rather tear-jerking consideration,
wouldn't you say?

14:03.200 --> 14:04.450
I see.

14:04.450 --> 14:06.380
So this is where you've been...

14:06.380 --> 14:07.480
Anri.

14:10.210 --> 14:15.410
At last, the time has come for me to 
unleash my ultimate twin-spear technique...

14:15.870 --> 14:19.580
<b>Ultimate Twin-Spear Technique:
Wicked Dragon Burial Twin Spear Wave</b>

14:15.870 --> 14:19.580
Ultimate Twin-Spear Technique: 
Wicked Dragon Burial Twin Spear Wave!

14:21.110 --> 14:23.310
You beat them already?!

14:23.310 --> 14:26.900
I'd expect no less from the legend 
who's slain over a hundred demons!

14:26.900 --> 14:28.800
<i>A formidable rival, this horse.</i>

14:28.800 --> 14:30.550
Even with my noble goal of seeing a naked—

14:30.550 --> 14:33.400
Rather, my goal of returning peace
to my city,

14:33.400 --> 14:36.390
I never would have made it this far alone.

14:36.760 --> 14:40.050
I used to be a merchant, you see.

14:40.050 --> 14:42.230
And one of my remaining 
wares from that time...

14:43.170 --> 14:45.780
is this little enchanted skiff.

14:45.780 --> 14:49.030
This will allow us to report to the king 
about the naked-in-stockings—

14:49.730 --> 14:53.030
I mean, about the situation 
in the city within the day!

14:53.710 --> 14:55.570
I just felt the most curious chill...

14:55.570 --> 14:57.150
<i>Stuffy-nose bestie!</i>

14:57.150 --> 14:59.000
What is the meaning of this?

14:59.000 --> 15:01.250
Well, a lot happened...

15:01.250 --> 15:03.210
Do you have a death wish?

15:03.210 --> 15:06.070
If I catch you eating someone, I'll kill you.

15:06.070 --> 15:07.420
How many times must I say it?

15:07.420 --> 15:10.250
<i>She has the devils firmly under her thumb.</i>

15:10.880 --> 15:13.020
<i>Even if she is Touka's master,</i>

15:13.020 --> 15:16.360
<i>surely it's perilous to trust this woman.</i>

15:16.360 --> 15:18.160
Ethel Borgnine...

15:18.160 --> 15:21.940
Head of the bandits wanted in the capital.

15:21.940 --> 15:25.740
And you're Fieri Yunis, 
formerly of the Four Knights.

15:25.740 --> 15:28.230
You're on my personal shit list, you know.

15:28.230 --> 15:29.580
What a coincidence.

15:29.580 --> 15:32.590
You happen to be on my grope list as well.

15:32.590 --> 15:33.740
All right, that's it.

15:33.740 --> 15:34.880
I'm killing you here and now!

15:34.880 --> 15:36.890
Then I'll grope you here and now!

15:36.890 --> 15:37.580
Knock it off!

15:37.580 --> 15:38.930
You're weirdly talking past each other!

15:38.930 --> 15:41.000
Also, we're working together right now!

15:41.770 --> 15:43.410
There it is.

15:43.410 --> 15:45.750
That's the magical craftsman's workshop.

15:45.750 --> 15:47.250
Get lost!

15:47.250 --> 15:49.590
I'm retired!

15:52.100 --> 15:53.890
Well, I got you to the workshop.

15:53.890 --> 15:55.470
The rest is in your hands.

15:55.470 --> 15:57.150
That wasn't the damn deal!

15:57.150 --> 15:58.520
He says he's retired!

15:59.800 --> 16:02.230
Goodness me. If you insist...

16:02.230 --> 16:04.240
If he won't let us in, 
we'll let ourselves in

16:04.240 --> 16:05.730
and steal a new enchanted carriage.

16:05.730 --> 16:07.960
All in the interest of saving people!

16:07.960 --> 16:09.400
We can't break the law!

16:09.400 --> 16:11.300
My Yuna's turned delinquent...

16:11.300 --> 16:12.610
Papa, get a grip!

16:13.350 --> 16:15.610
Now I'm complicit!

16:16.900 --> 16:18.870
You filthy criminals!

16:18.870 --> 16:21.550
I trust you're prepared to die!

16:22.670 --> 16:24.580
Sion! Is that you, Sion?!

16:24.580 --> 16:27.130
Hey, you old coot! I ain't Sion!

16:27.130 --> 16:27.970
Forgive me.

16:27.970 --> 16:29.560
My vision's grown so poor, you see...

16:29.560 --> 16:31.670
You just had the air of Sion about you.

16:31.670 --> 16:33.870
Are you a fan of Sir Sion's?

16:33.870 --> 16:35.890
Oh, I forgot to mention it.

16:35.890 --> 16:38.260
This is Ledo Breydan.

16:36.640 --> 16:40.350
<b>Ledo Breydan
Sion's Grandfather</b>

16:38.260 --> 16:40.350
He's Sion the hero's grandfather.

16:40.350 --> 16:41.680
Forgive me.

16:41.680 --> 16:43.560
My vision's grown so poor, you see...

16:44.010 --> 16:47.400
If I'd known it was you, Sion, 
I'd have let you right in.

16:47.400 --> 16:49.020
The damn cup's right there!

16:49.020 --> 16:53.710
I'm told he swore to focus on nothing 
but his battle until the world is safe.

16:53.710 --> 16:55.820
Is that why he's so quiet?

16:55.820 --> 16:57.990
That's my good, obedient boy.

16:57.990 --> 17:01.200
Look, can you fix our 
enchanted carriage up quick?

17:01.200 --> 17:04.460
I can swap the broken rear wheel 
and magical channels quickly enough,

17:04.460 --> 17:06.920
but repairs to the enchanted 
engine may prove difficult.

17:06.920 --> 17:10.620
With my stamina and vision 
in this sorry state,

17:10.620 --> 17:12.880
it could take two whole days!

17:12.880 --> 17:14.220
Two days?!

17:14.220 --> 17:16.130
That's too damn slow!

17:16.130 --> 17:17.840
Got any other carriages lying around?

17:17.840 --> 17:21.810
None that would reach Elvania within a day.

17:22.100 --> 17:23.270
This is terrible...

17:23.770 --> 17:24.600
Mr. Ledo.

17:25.030 --> 17:28.680
I've digested an introductory volume 
on magical craftsmanship.

17:28.680 --> 17:31.860
How much more should I read 
if I wish to assist you?

17:31.860 --> 17:34.470
Truly? In such a short time?

17:34.470 --> 17:36.320
I'm a very fast learner.

17:36.320 --> 17:38.010
I see...

17:38.010 --> 17:40.050
This here should just about do it.

17:40.050 --> 17:41.280
Very well.

17:41.690 --> 17:45.000
Please give me approximately 
an hour and a half.

17:45.000 --> 17:47.480
Damn, Marguerite's something else!

17:47.480 --> 17:49.500
What's her brain even made of?

17:49.500 --> 17:51.700
That's a princess for you!

17:51.700 --> 17:54.830
By the way, what's the deal with 
you being a "legendary hero"?

17:54.830 --> 17:56.000
And your Sacred Sword—

17:56.000 --> 17:58.570
That's right. We never got around to that.

17:58.570 --> 18:02.230
But I can't reveal such 
information to an enemy.

18:02.230 --> 18:05.380
Oh? Now I'm even more curious.

18:05.380 --> 18:06.850
If you tell me, I might give you—

18:07.040 --> 18:08.500
A feel? Of boobies?!

18:08.500 --> 18:11.110
Give me a handful of those puppies,
and I'll gladly tell you!

18:11.110 --> 18:12.750
I was going to say information!

18:12.750 --> 18:14.070
Intel on your enemy!

18:14.940 --> 18:16.210
Very well.

18:16.210 --> 18:17.030
Milly.

18:17.480 --> 18:19.110
It's a man-made Sacred Sword.

18:19.110 --> 18:23.750
Mages and magical craftsmen from 
all over the world worked together

18:23.750 --> 18:26.580
to make four new Sacred Swords. 
This is one of them.

18:26.580 --> 18:28.130
A man-made Sacred Sword?!

18:28.130 --> 18:31.880
You mean that sword could 
seal the Gates of Hell too?

18:31.880 --> 18:35.880
No, the man-made Sacred Swords 
aren't quite that potent.

18:35.880 --> 18:38.550
So how's it different from a normal sword?

18:38.550 --> 18:39.930
I see...

18:39.930 --> 18:43.330
That Sacred Sword could slay the 
Dark Lord and his Four Infernal Generals?

18:43.330 --> 18:45.270
Yes, that's right.

18:45.270 --> 18:48.020
Given the Generals' remarkable
regenerative powers,

18:48.020 --> 18:51.630
all arms but the legendary Sacred Sword
are ineffective against them.

18:51.630 --> 18:55.480
But if this blade can slay them,
that truly would make you a hero.

18:55.480 --> 18:59.320
The intel I have to offer also 
concerns the Infernal Generals.

18:59.320 --> 19:03.280
The necromancers you're up against...

19:03.280 --> 19:06.290
They have the bodies of the Infernal 
Generals in their possession.

19:06.760 --> 19:11.000
In addition, over a thousand devils 
await you in Elvania.

19:11.000 --> 19:15.690
You'll have to beat every single 
one of them within the day.

19:15.690 --> 19:19.970
Surely that makes the gravity
of the fight ahead of you clear.

19:19.970 --> 19:23.550
If you don't want to die, 
you should give up right now.

19:23.550 --> 19:26.930
The Four Infernal Generals... 
and a thousand devils?

19:26.930 --> 19:30.170
Or we can bypass Elvania
and hit the Gates of Hell.

19:30.170 --> 19:35.500
It's not like you really care about saving
people or the fate of the world, right?

19:36.860 --> 19:39.320
We've got the legendary hero, his companions,

19:39.320 --> 19:41.510
and a former member 
of the Four Knights with us.

19:41.510 --> 19:44.070
We'll kick their asses,
no matter what they throw at us.

19:44.670 --> 19:46.530
Do you really mean that?

19:48.320 --> 19:51.980
It's true that I don't have a scrap 
of do-gooder in me.

19:51.980 --> 19:55.460
But this is just like three
and a half years ago.

19:57.610 --> 20:01.530
I'm trying to save the same person now.

20:07.540 --> 20:09.390
The person you're trying to save...

20:09.390 --> 20:10.890
Is it my big sister?

20:12.350 --> 20:13.680
Yeah.

20:13.680 --> 20:16.310
She's been infected with 
a devil-conversion spell.

20:16.310 --> 20:19.570
The reason I'm in her body is to 
keep her from going on a rampage.

20:20.010 --> 20:21.280
That's awful...

20:21.280 --> 20:24.770
But running into you 
means we're in the clear!

20:24.770 --> 20:27.330
I was worried we couldn't
hack this on our own.

20:27.330 --> 20:29.240
Plus, you've got that awesome sword!

20:29.240 --> 20:32.120
How'd you get your hands on it, anyway?

20:32.520 --> 20:36.080
I won a tournament held 
in the western kingdom

20:36.080 --> 20:39.210
and was thus declared a legendary
hero worthy of wielding it.

20:39.580 --> 20:42.060
Hey, want to duel for old time's sake?

20:42.060 --> 20:44.430
With our future marriage on the line!

20:45.640 --> 20:46.710
The hell?!

20:46.710 --> 20:49.560
Hang on, this can't possibly 
be the best time for—

20:53.230 --> 20:55.440
Now you're shooting at me?!

20:55.440 --> 20:58.900
The projectiles come from my sword, 
so it's allowed!

20:58.900 --> 21:00.690
You're gonna freakin' kill me!

21:00.690 --> 21:02.880
Then we'll be married in the afterlife!

21:05.360 --> 21:07.570
Damn it! If that's how you wanna play...

21:07.570 --> 21:10.990
Sorry, but I'll just knock you out cold!

21:12.450 --> 21:14.710
<i>Crap. My mana's totally...</i>

21:19.250 --> 21:21.380
I-I lose, okay?

21:21.380 --> 21:23.630
But you gotta beat me 
a hundred times to marry me, so—

21:23.630 --> 21:27.090
You'll "kick their asses"?
You're "in the clear"?

21:27.520 --> 21:31.210
How are you going to save my 
sister when you're this weak?!

21:31.210 --> 21:33.430
You're clearly not facing reality!

21:37.540 --> 21:39.440
I'm still going to save her.

21:39.440 --> 21:44.400
I'll use whatever dirty, 
underhanded tricks I have to.

21:44.400 --> 21:47.360
This is no different from three years ago.

21:47.720 --> 21:50.950
The legendary hero saved you back then.

21:51.830 --> 21:54.040
But now, the legendary hero is dead...

21:54.040 --> 21:56.660
So who's going to save her if I don't?

21:57.720 --> 21:59.130
I'm glad.

21:59.130 --> 22:01.590
I knew that's what you'd say.

22:02.470 --> 22:04.630
H-Hang on, you did that on purpose?

22:04.630 --> 22:06.500
I know how it went down.

22:06.500 --> 22:12.100
Three years ago, you were the one
who really saved us, weren't you?

22:12.580 --> 22:15.910
I had a chance to ask Sion, and he told me.

22:16.310 --> 22:20.020
When the devils attacked Elvania, 
the reason he was able to make it in time

22:20.020 --> 22:22.980
was because of all the traps 
set along on the way!

22:23.300 --> 22:25.270
So if this is no different from back then,

22:25.270 --> 22:28.350
you'll be the one to save her again!

22:28.750 --> 22:29.950
Nah.

22:30.360 --> 22:33.410
All I did back then was buy time.

22:33.410 --> 22:36.370
We'd have been helpless 
if the hero hadn't shown up.

22:36.370 --> 22:38.150
That said...

22:38.150 --> 22:40.580
I'm not the guy I was three years ago.

22:40.580 --> 22:42.540
I've got the legendary hero's power.

22:42.830 --> 22:44.750
I've got friends I can trust.

22:44.750 --> 22:47.340
So this time, I really will be the one to...

22:47.340 --> 22:49.970
<i>We'll</i> be the ones to save Yuna!

22:49.970 --> 22:52.430
Of course we will!

22:52.430 --> 22:55.390
Boy, none of this sounds like me, does it?

22:55.390 --> 22:57.310
I'm gonna hit the crapper.

22:57.310 --> 22:59.070
I've been holding it in this whole time.

22:59.070 --> 23:00.600
Yeah, sure!

23:05.980 --> 23:09.740
<i>Yeah, I've been holding in 
the urge all this time...</i>

23:10.840 --> 23:12.680
<i>No matter what anyone tells me,</i>

23:12.680 --> 23:16.660
<i>I have no choice </i>but<i> to save Yuna.</i>

23:16.660 --> 23:21.810
<i>Rather, there's something even more
precious than Yuna I have to protect...</i>

23:21.810 --> 23:23.870
<i>It's these pretty li'l thighs!</i>

23:23.870 --> 23:26.990
<i>Yeah, Yuna's thighs are the best!</i>

23:26.990 --> 23:30.920
<i>The ultimate thighs, combining sexiness 
and beauty in one tight package!</i>

23:30.920 --> 23:34.170
<i>This creamy softness from 
which all kindness flows...</i>

23:34.170 --> 23:36.510
<i>They could suck my entire body in—</i>

23:36.510 --> 23:39.980
<b>18 hours until Yuna and the others become devils</b>
